questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot REST API slowly consumes heap memory over time, eventually crashing with `java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space`. A heap dump analysis reveals millions of `UserContext` instances retained in memory. You inspect the following custom interceptor snippet:

java
@Component
public class ContextInterceptor implements HandlerInterceptor {
    private static final ThreadLocal<UserContext> contextHolder = new ThreadLocal<>();

    @Override
    public boolean preHandle(HttpServletRequest request, HttpServletResponse response, Object handler) {
        String userId = request.getHeader("X-User-ID");
        if (userId != null) {
            contextHolder.set(new UserContext(userId));
        }
        return true;
    }
}
